<p>
That's it. ~100 lines. No dependencies. No packages to manage! (well except ripgrep of course)
</p>

<p>
Now that I have complete control over this function, I have added further improvements over rgrep, inspired by <code>deadgrep</code>
</p>

<ul class="org-ul">
<li><b><code>S</code></b> - New search term</li>
<li><b><code>D</code></b> - New directory</li>
<li><b><code>o</code></b> - New glob pattern</li>
<li><b><code>g</code></b> - Re-run current search</li>
</ul>

<p>
and a universal argument can be passed through to set these up on the initial grep
</p>

<p>
I have tried to make the output as similar as possible to rgrep, to be compatible with <code>grep-mode</code> and for familiarity, so it will be something like:
</p>

